Root cause:
The bug was caused by the logic that ignored short lines (less than 3 characters) in the `parse_file` function. This led to a situation where a short line could unintentionally continue the previous line if it was part of a continuation, resulting in incorrect parsing of udev rules. The patch corrects this by ensuring that short lines are not ignored, thus preventing them from being treated as continuations of the previous line.
